meta {
  name: Stream Transactions
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: grpc.mainnet.aptoslabs.com:443
  method: /aptos.indexer.v1.RawData/GetTransactions
  body: grpc
  protoPath: grpc/proto/aptos/indexer/v1/raw_data.proto
  auth: inherit
  methodType: server-streaming
}

metadata {
  authorization: Bearer {{aptos_api_key}}
}

body:grpc {
  name: message 1
  content: '''
    {
      "starting_version": "0",
      "transactions_count": "10"
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  Streams transactions from the Aptos blockchain starting from a specific
  version, using the Aptos Labs hosted Transaction Stream Service.

  **Service:** `aptos.indexer.v1.RawData`
  **Method:** `GetTransactions` (server-streaming)

  For the same stream served through Alchemy endpoints, use the request in
  the `grpc/` folder instead.

  Request Parameters:
  - starting_version: The ledger version to start streaming from (optional)
    - If not provided, starts from the latest version
    - Can be set to 0 to stream from genesis
  - transactions_count: Total number of transactions to stream before the
    stream ends (optional; omit for an infinite live stream)
  - batch_size: Number of transactions per response message (default: 1000)

  Response:
  - Stream of TransactionsResponse messages containing batches of transactions
  - Each transaction includes:
    - Version, hash, sender, type
    - Payload (entry function, script, or module bundle)
    - Gas information
    - Success status and VM status
    - Events and state changes
    - Signature information

  Authentication:
  - Requires `authorization: Bearer <key>` header (set `aptos_api_key` in
    your Bruno environment)
  - Get an API key from https://developers.aptoslabs.com/

  Use Cases:
  - Real-time transaction monitoring
  - Building custom indexers
  - Event tracking and notifications
  - Analytics and data processing

  https://aptos.dev/build/indexer/txn-stream
  https://aptos.dev/build/indexer/txn-stream/aptos-hosted-txn-stream
}
